			"Message": "build(Output): Update source map for Blob URL rewrite transform\n\nSynchronize the JavaScript source map file for the `InjectWebviewBlobUrlRewrite` plugin following recent code changes. This ensures debugging fidelity and accurate stack trace mapping for the runtime script injected into extension webviews to handle cross-protocol asset loading in WKWebView.\n\nThe update reflects the latest transformation logic without altering the compiled JavaScript output.",
			"SHA": "92474f945fd4002d85400051d7a0a3fcd39e6b22"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T00:57:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				7
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Inject Blob URL rewrite for extension webviews in WKWebView\n\nAddress a critical failure mode in WKWebView where extension panels (e.g., Roo Code) remain blank due to cross-protocol security restrictions. The inner iframe, sandboxed under `vscode-webview://`, cannot load resources via `vscode-file://` or `vscode-webview-resource://` schemes, causing React bundles to never execute.\n\nIntroduce `InjectWebviewBlobUrlRewrite` into the Output build pipeline (`Source/Plugin` and `Configuration/Plugin`). This transform injects a runtime script into `pre/index.html` that intercepts `Document.prototype.write` calls from the outer shell. The script parses incoming HTML, fetches assets with `vscode-*` schemes from the privileged outer context, converts them to stable `blob:` URLs, and rewrites the DOM before injection. Includes a per-URL cache to handle extension reloads efficiently.\n\nThe plugin is positioned after `PatchWebviewIframeServiceWorker` and before `RewriteWebviewShellCSP` to ensure correct pipeline ordering and CSP compliance. Execution is guarded by the `__LAND_WEBVIEW_BLOB_URL_REWRITE__` marker to maintain idempotency.",
			"SHA": "a4414f3d3d0057c707685e3c2f15af0c1ff38f11"
		},
		{
			"Author": "github-actions[bot]",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T00:42:13Z",
